<title>ARGENTINA: MOTOR RACING-VILLENEUVE WINS ARGENTINE GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-VILLENEUVE WINS ARGENTINE GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Jacques Villeneuve, driving a Williams, won the Argentine Grand Prix motor race on Sunday.  </p>
<p>Eddie Irvine of Britain was second in a Ferrari and Ralf</p>
<p>Schumacher of German third in a Jordan.</p>
<p>Britain's Johnny Herbert finished fourth in a Sauber, Mikka</p>
<p>Hakkinen of Finland fifth in a McLaren and Gerhard Berger of</p>
<p>Austria sixth in a Benetton.</p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after three rounds):</p>
<p> 1. Villeneuve				20 points</p>
<p>2. equal. David Coulthard (Britain)  10</p>
<p> 2. equal. Berger			   10</p>
<p> 4. Hakkinen				   9</p>
<p> 5. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	 8</p>
<p> 6 equal. Oliver Panis (France)	  6</p>
<p> 6 equal. Irvine			     6</p>
<p> 8. Ralf Schumacher			  4</p>
<p> 9. Herbert				    3</p>
<p> 10 equal. Nicola Larini (Italy)	 1</p>
<p> 10 equal. Jean Alessi (France)	  1</p>
<p>Constructors' championship:</p>
<p> 1. Williams				  20 points</p>
<p> 2. McLaren-Mercedes			19</p>
<p> 3. Ferrari				   14</p>
<p> 4. Benetton-Renault			11</p>
<p> 5. Prost					6</p>
<p> 6 equal. Sauber-Petronas		  4</p>
<p> 6 equal. Jordan			     4</p>
<p>Next round: San Marino, April 27</p>
</text>
